They provide jsonq, a small JSON path query tool (no jq, no Python) that the test and
build scripts use. The rest of zclassicd remains under the MIT license (see COPYING).
Vendored files must never be edited in this tree. Provenance and identity checks:
src/c23/tools/check-vendor.sh zcutil/tools/Z23_SOURCE.tsv  (make -C src check-tools-vendor).
